window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-345ff9b5b21e3cd8"]={"key":"ny_b1-345ff9b5b21e3cd8","group":"ny_b1","uid":"345ff9b5b21e3cd8","rank":95,"title":"fern001 conformance opinion","occupation":"mechanical_engineers","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Tadeo Okonkwo, the manufacturing engineer at Fernhollow Systems who designed the weld fixture for Sandpiper Supply's chassis line. Sandpiper is rejecting parts against the flatness callout, and Noor Maldonado needs a firm position for the claim meeting with Sandpiper. Use `award_drawing_and_tolerance.pdf` and `inspection_bundle.xlsx` to prepare `sandpiper_conformance_opinion.docx` and `sandpiper_conformance_register.xlsx`; write both files into the top level of the working directory using exactly those filenames. Give a clear yes-or-no conclusion on whether the rejected parts conform under the supplied award documents, rather than a balanced discussion. The letter should be suitable to send to the commercial lead, identify the drawing and tolerance basis, state which inspection evidence you relied on and which you did not, and disclose that you designed the fixture. Explain briefly how you insulated the opinion from that conflict. In the workbook, preserve a traceable evidence register and show the treatment of duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, or inconsistently labelled entries. Do not bring in later standards, customer concessions, or assumptions not supported by the two supplied files, and make the letter and workbook agree wherever they state the same fact.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/award_drawing_and_tolerance.pdf` — Award-time drawing extract and tolerance text governing the chassis fixture, including the datum reference frame, manufacturing sequence, surface identification, and contractual scope.\n- `references/inspection_bundle.xlsx` — Mixed inspection and rejection evidence supplied by the quality team, including measurement rows, notes, labels, status fields, and an unrelated contact table placed beside the evidence table.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `sandpiper_conformance_opinion.docx` — A concise conformance opinion letter for Noor Maldonado containing a committed conclusion, source basis, evidence treatment, limitations, and conflict-of-interest disclosure. (Use only facts supported by the two supplied reference files.; State a clear yes-or-no position on conformity under the award documents.; Identify the applicable drawing feature, datum scheme, tolerance, inspection basis, exclusions, and material limitations.; Disclose Tadeo Okonkwo's role in designing the fixture and explain the safeguard used to insulate the review.; Make every figure and factual statement shared with the workbook agree with it.; Do not cite external standards or invent customer concessions, dates, people, organisations, or measurements.)\n- `sandpiper_conformance_register.xlsx` — A traceable evidence register showing the source rows considered, normalized labels, inclusion or exclusion decisions, reasons, measurements, and the basis for the final conclusion. (Retain traceability to source row identifiers or equivalent source locations.; Show how duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, and inconsistently labelled records were handled.; Distinguish the drawing-controlled inspection surface from measurements taken on another surface.; Do not silently invent values for unusable records.; Make all summary figures and conclusion fields agree with the opinion letter.; Avoid external data and do not reproduce the unrelated contact table as inspection evidence.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/award_drawing_and_tolerance.pdf","bytes":2798,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/9bc1ed4b52d1c0f010ec498543f3d729c7bb1a012e404b002c96cc5dc282026b.pdf","sha256":"9bc1ed4b52d1c0f010ec498543f3d729c7bb1a012e404b002c96cc5dc282026b","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"          FERNHOLLOW SYSTEMS — AWARD DRAWING EXTRACT\nSandpiper Supply chassis-line weld fixture\nDrawing ID: FH-SS-CHS-017      Revision: B   Issue date: 14 May 2024\n\n    Feature / datum                  Definition in award drawing\n    Datum A                          Finished machined face (primary plane)\n    Datum B                          Locating feature used with datum A after machining\n    Datum C                          Locating feature used with datum A and B after machining\n    Flatness feature control frame0.18 mm applied to the finished machined face\n\n\n\nManufacturing sequence\nWelding precedes machining. The as-welded assembly face is not the finished controlled surface. The flatness callout is evaluated on the\nfinished machined face using the supplied datum reference frame A|B|C.\n\n\n\nContractual scope note\nThis supplied award drawing and the companion tolerance text are the governing contract documents for this review. No later revision,\ncustomer concession, or external standard is incorporated in this extract.\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/inspection_bundle.xlsx","bytes":6647,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/c6bf552c6822db38efd01618e9190b6e4f94835d5022de9540b6b535f002179c.xlsx","sha256":"c6bf552c6822db38efd01618e9190b6e4f94835d5022de9540b6b535f002179c","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Inspection Export","row_count":19,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SANDPIPER SUPPLY — QUALITY EXPORT"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Export scope: chassis fixture flatness checks | received 16 May 2024 09:42 UTC"]},{"r":"4","cells":["","","","Evidence table begins below; gutter columns A:C retained from export layout","","","","","","","","","CONTACT ROUTING (unrelated)"]},{"r":"5","cells":["","","","","","","","","","","","","Cust ID","customer_name","Escalation\nphone","Region"]},{"r":"6","cells":["","","","Source ID","Part ID","Surface label","Datum ref","Measured flatness","Unit","Disposition","Notes","","SS-01","Noor Maldonado","+1 555 010 0198","West"]},{"r":"7","cells":["","","","EV-001","CH-104","finished face","A|B|C","0.11","mm","Accept","","","FH-02","Inez Calder","+1 555 010 0134","Central"]},{"r":"8","cells":["","","","EV-002","CH-105","machined surface","A|B|C","0.14","mm","Accept",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["","","","EV-003","CH-106","finished machined face","A|B|C","0.16","mm","Accept",""]},{"r":"10","cells":["","","","EV-004","CH-107","finished face","A|B|C","0.09","mm","Accept","Setup check; non-production piece"]},{"r":"11","cells":["","","","EV-005","CH-108","as-welded face","A|B|C","0.24","mm","Reject",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["","","","EV-006","CH-109","as welded face","A|B|C","0.21","mm","Reject",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["","","","EV-007","CH-110","machined surface","A|B|C","0.15?","mm","Reject","Instrument text includes qualifier; no valid numeric reading"]},{"r":"14","cells":["","","","EV-008","CH-111","finished face","A|B|C","0.12","mm","Accept",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["","","","EV-009","CH-112","finished machined face","A|B|C","0.17","mm","Accept",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["","","","EV-010","CH-113","finished face","A|B|C","0.1","mm","Accept",""]},{"r":"17","cells":["","","","EV-011","CH-113","finished face","A|B|C","0.1","mm","Accept","Repeat of EV-010: same part and inspection event"]},{"r":"18","cells":["","","","EV-012","CH-114","edge profile","A|B|C","0.07000000000000001","mm","Accept","Profile characteristic, not flatness"]},{"r":"19","cells":["","","","EV-013","CH-115","machined surface","A|B|C","","mm","Pending","No valid reading recorded"]},{"r":"20","cells":["","","","EV-014","CH-116","finished face","A|B|C","0.13","mm","Accept",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/sandpiper_conformance_opinion.docx","bytes":37965,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/9bfb5bcf50a62d5a134f41541057052bf4c29f2780294b63e1982a12f009eb8b.docx","sha256":"9bfb5bcf50a62d5a134f41541057052bf4c29f2780294b63e1982a12f009eb8b","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"FERNHOLLOW SYSTEMS\nSandpiper Supply chassis-line flatness conformance opinion\nTo: Noor Maldonado, Commercial Lead\nFrom: Tadeo Okonkwo, Manufacturing Engineer\nSubject: Award-document position on rejected chassis-line parts\nConclusion — YES. The rejected parts conform under the supplied award drawing and tolerance text. The contractual 0.18 mm flatness callout governs the finished machined face (datum A), and the valid controlled-face evidence is within that limit.\nBasis. I relied on award drawing FH-SS-CHS-017, Revision B, issued 14 May 2024, and its companion tolerance text. Datum A is the finished machined face; datum B and datum C are locating features in the supplied datum reference frame A|B|C. The drawing states that welding precedes machining, so the flatness callout applies to the finished machined face rather than the as-welded assembly face.\nEvidence. I reviewed the evidence table in inspection_bundle.xlsx row by row. After applying note overrides, removing the repeated EV-011 event, excluding the setup-check piece EV-004, excluding malformed EV-007, excluding irrelevant profile row EV-012, and leaving EV-013 unresolved because it has no valid reading, 7 distinct usable controlled-face records remain. Their flatness values are 0.10 mm minimum, 0.17 mm maximum, and 0.133 mm arithmetic mean. The maximum is below 0.18 mm.\nThe as-welded readings EV-005 (0.24 mm) and EV-006 (0.21 mm) were not used to establish failure. They are measurements of a different, pre-machining surface; an as-welded exceedance therefore cannot establish nonconformance against the finished machined-face callout. The register records those exclusions and every other reviewed row.\nConflict disclosure and safeguard. I designed the Fernhollow Systems weld fixture under review. To insulate this opinion from that potential self-interest, I used only the supplied award documents and a reproducible row-selection method: normalize surface labels, let free-text notes override conflicting fields, remove duplicate events, and calculate statistics solely from included controlled-face readings. The commercial or quality team can reproduce each decision from the source row and reason recorded in the register; no unsupported assurance from me is used.\nLimitations. This opinion is limited to the supplied FH-SS-CHS-017 Rev B award drawing/tolerance text and inspection_bundle.xlsx evidence. It does not incorporate later standards, customer concessions, revisions, or other contractual terms. EV-007 and EV-013 remain unusable for numeric comparison rather than being estimated.\nRegards,\n\nTadeo Okonkwo\nManufacturing Engineer\nFernhollow Systems","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/private/gold/sandpiper_conformance_register.xlsx","bytes":8272,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/0e430267b662282c3764d6297404486c160b3670784e001d38cfa88d21e54d73.xlsx","sha256":"0e430267b662282c3764d6297404486c160b3670784e001d38cfa88d21e54d73","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Conformance Register","row_count":28,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["SANDPIPER CONFORMANCE REGISTER"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Award basis: FH-SS-CHS-017 Rev B (14 May 2024) | Inspection source: inspection_bundle.xlsx"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Conclusion","YES — rejected parts conform under the supplied award documents."]},{"r":"5","cells":["Controlled surface","Datum A: finished machined face; B and C are locating features."]},{"r":"6","cells":["Flatness tolerance","0.18 mm"]},{"r":"7","cells":["Included controlled-face records","7"]},{"r":"8","cells":["Minimum (mm)","0.1"]},{"r":"9","cells":["Maximum (mm)","0.17"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Arithmetic mean (mm)","0.1328571428571429"]},{"r":"11","cells":["Maximum vs tolerance","0.17 mm \u003c= 0.18 mm — PASS"]},{"r":"12","cells":["As-welded treatment","Excluded from contractual calculation; as-welded face is not the controlled finished surface."]},{"r":"13","cells":["Conflict safeguard","Tadeo Okonkwo designed the fixture. Review applies the drawing and row-selection rules consistently; the register is reproducible by commercial/quality reviewers."]},{"r":"14","cells":["Scope limitation","Limited to the supplied award drawing/tolerance text and inspection bundle; no later standards or concessions used."]},{"r":"16","cells":["Source row / ID","Part ID","Original surface label","Normalized surface","Datum ref","Source measured value","Unit","Source disposition","Source notes","Final decision","Decision reason"]},{"r":"17","cells":["EV-001","CH-104","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.11","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"18","cells":["EV-002","CH-105","machined surface","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.14","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"19","cells":["EV-003","CH-106","finished machined face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.16","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"20","cells":["EV-004","CH-107","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.09","mm","Accept","Setup check; non-production piece","Excluded - non-production","Free-text note overrides Accept status: setup check/non-production piece"]},{"r":"21","cells":["EV-005","CH-108","as-welded face","As-welded assembly face","A|B|C","0.24","mm","Reject","","Excluded - as-welded","As-welded surface is not the finished machined face controlled by the 0.18 mm callout"]},{"r":"22","cells":["EV-006","CH-109","as welded face","As-welded assembly face","A|B|C","0.21","mm","Reject","","Excluded - as-welded","As-welded surface is not the finished machined face controlled by the 0.18 mm callout"]},{"r":"23","cells":["EV-007","CH-110","machined surface","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.15?","mm","Reject","Instrument text includes qualifier; no valid numeric reading","Malformed - excluded","Source measurement contains qualifier (0.15?); not a defensible numeric value"]},{"r":"24","cells":["EV-008","CH-111","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.12","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"25","cells":["EV-009","CH-112","finished machined face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.17","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"26","cells":["EV-010","CH-113","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.1","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]},{"r":"27","cells":["EV-011","CH-113","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.1","mm","Accept","Repeat of EV-010: same part and inspection event","Duplicate - excluded","Duplicate of EV-010 (same part and inspection event); prevents double counting"]},{"r":"28","cells":["EV-012","CH-114","edge profile","Other / irrelevant characteristic","A|B|C","0.07000000000000001","mm","Accept","Profile characteristic, not flatness","Irrelevant - excluded","Different inspection characteristic (profile), not contractual flatness"]},{"r":"29","cells":["EV-013","CH-115","machined surface","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","","mm","Pending","No valid reading recorded","Unresolved - excluded","No valid measurement supplied; left blank without estimate"]},{"r":"30","cells":["EV-014","CH-116","finished face","Controlled finished machined face","A|B|C","0.13","mm","Accept","","Included","Usable numeric reading on drawing-controlled finished machined face"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX contains the exact deliverable subject or equivalent wording identifying the Sandpiper Supply chassis-line flatness conformance opinion.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX text.","grader_hint":"Confirm the document is plainly an opinion about the specified chassis-line flatness issue, not a generic quality report."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies Fernhollow Systems and Sandpiper Supply correctly.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text.","grader_hint":"Check organisation names against the supplied sources and request."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies Tadeo Okonkwo as the author or reviewing manufacturing engineer.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text.","grader_hint":"Verify the named engineer is present without an invented person."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies the supplied award drawing and tolerance text as the governing basis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit award-document limitation, not merely a generic reference to a drawing."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states a direct affirmative conformity conclusion rather than presenting only alternatives or a balanced discussion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conclusion paragraph in DOCX.","grader_hint":"The conclusion must say the rejected parts conform under the supplied award documents or equivalent unambiguous affirmative wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX's affirmative conclusion is tied to the drawing-controlled finished machined face, not merely to the existence of any passing measurement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conclusion and reasoning paragraphs compared with PDF and register.","grader_hint":"Require an explicit logical link between the controlled surface and conformity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies datum A as the finished machined face.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent terminology only if it clearly denotes datum A and the finished machined face."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies datum B as a locating feature in the supplied datum reference frame.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Check that B is not mislabeled as the controlled surface."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies datum C as a locating feature in the supplied datum reference frame.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Check that C is not omitted or misidentified."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states the flatness tolerance value and unit as supplied.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Compare the literal value and unit with the PDF; do not accept a bare or unitless number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states that the flatness callout applies to the finished machined face rather than the as-welded assembly face.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Drawing-basis paragraph.","grader_hint":"This is the central interpretation; it must be explicit, not inferred only from a copied datum label."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states that welding precedes machining or otherwise accurately describes the supplied manufacturing sequence.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text compared with PDF.","grader_hint":"Check sequence wording against the drawing note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX explains why an as-welded measurement cannot establish nonconformance against the machined-face flatness callout.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reasoning paragraph and register decisions.","grader_hint":"Require the surface mismatch to be explained, not just named."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX distinguishes valid controlled-face measurements from as-welded measurements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence summary.","grader_hint":"A single undifferentiated measurement total fails this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX reports the valid controlled-face record count equal to the distinct non-duplicate, usable records for the drawing-controlled surface, within ±0 records.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX summary compared with scripted source derivation.","grader_hint":"Count after notes overrides, duplicate removal, and exclusion of malformed or irrelevant records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX reports the valid controlled-face minimum equal to the source-derived minimum, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX summary and source workbook.","grader_hint":"Use only usable controlled-face records after normalization and exception handling."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX reports the valid controlled-face maximum equal to the source-derived maximum, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX summary and source workbook.","grader_hint":"Check the maximum is not taken from the as-welded or excluded records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX reports the valid controlled-face arithmetic mean equal to the source-derived mean, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX summary and source workbook.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from distinct usable controlled-face measurements; accept rounding within the stated tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The reported controlled-face maximum is at or below the supplied flatness tolerance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX and PDF.","grader_hint":"Compare the reported maximum and tolerance numerically, allowing the R17 tolerance only for displayed rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies the inspection bundle as the source of the measurement evidence.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX text.","grader_hint":"Require a source reference that a reviewer can follow."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX discloses that Tadeo Okonkwo designed the fixture under review.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Disclosure paragraph.","grader_hint":"The disclosure must be explicit and not hidden only in metadata or a signature."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The conflict disclosure and insulation explanation are credible, specific, and sufficient for a commercial claim letter.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"DOCX disclosure and methodology sections.","grader_hint":"Award only if the letter acknowledges the potential self-interest and describes a reproducible document-based safeguard rather than claiming objectivity without explanation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states that the opinion is limited to the supplied award documents and inspection evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or limitation paragraph.","grader_hint":"Check that later standards, concessions, and unsupported assumptions are expressly outside scope."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX does not rely on an external standard, later concession, or unsupplied contractual term to reach the conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Full DOCX text and cited sources.","grader_hint":"Treat external governing material as a failure; ordinary explanatory engineering language is acceptable if not presented as an additional rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX identifies at least one concrete limitation or unresolved evidence issue from the inspection bundle.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitations section.","grader_hint":"The statement must correspond to an actual malformed, unresolved, or otherwise excluded source record."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX states that the conclusion does not treat the as-welded exceedance as a failure of the drawing-controlled flatness requirement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reasoning and conclusion.","grader_hint":"This must be explicit enough to prevent a reader from interpreting the as-welded exceedance as the decisive result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX contains a traceability field linking each reviewed evidence decision to a source row or source location.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook headers and populated register.","grader_hint":"Check that traceability is row-level and usable, not only a general source note."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX includes every source evidence record in the review universe, including records later marked excluded, unresolved, duplicate, or irrelevant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Register compared with source evidence table.","grader_hint":"Reconcile source identifiers; a register containing only accepted rows fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX normalizes equivalent labels for the finished machined face into one clearly identified controlled-surface category.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Normalized surface field and method note.","grader_hint":"Accept any transparent mapping that groups the source's equivalent labels without grouping the as-welded label."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX keeps the as-welded surface distinct from the controlled machined surface.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Normalized surface field.","grader_hint":"Check all as-welded rows, including inconsistent labels, are not silently mapped to the controlled surface."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX applies the free-text notes as row-level exceptions when notes conflict with a main status, surface, or eligibility field.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Notes, decision, and reason columns.","grader_hint":"Inspect each seeded override and confirm the final decision follows the note rather than the conflicting main column."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX identifies the duplicate record and prevents it from contributing a second time to counts or summary statistics.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Duplicate flag, reason, and summary formulas or values.","grader_hint":"Check duplicate treatment against the source event identity and the register summary."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX identifies malformed measurement entries and prevents them from contributing an invented numeric value.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision and measurement fields.","grader_hint":"A malformed source value may be preserved as text, but it must not be converted into an unsupported number."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX identifies irrelevant rows and excludes them from the conformance calculation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Relevance or inclusion field and summary reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Check both the row decision and the summary population."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX leaves unsupported or unresolved measurements blank or explicitly unresolved rather than filling them with an estimate.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Register measurement and decision fields.","grader_hint":"Accept an explicit nonnumeric unresolved marker only if it is clearly not a measurement and is consistently explained."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX includes a final inclusion decision for every reviewed row.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision column populated across register.","grader_hint":"Every source row must be classifiable as included, excluded, duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, or unresolved as appropriate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every included numeric record in the XLSX is a usable measurement on the drawing-controlled machined face after notes and duplicate handling.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filter included rows and inspect normalized fields.","grader_hint":"Any included as-welded, duplicate, malformed, or irrelevant row fails this predicate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No excluded as-welded measurement contributes to the controlled-face count, minimum, maximum, or mean.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Register and summary reconciliation.","grader_hint":"Recompute all four metrics from included rows only."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX records the reason that as-welded measurements are excluded from the contractual flatness calculation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reason or method field.","grader_hint":"The reason must refer to the drawing-controlled machined face or equivalent source-grounded basis."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX records the reason for each duplicate exclusion or consolidation.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Row-level reason field.","grader_hint":"A generic 'excluded' label is insufficient for the duplicate row."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX records the reason for each malformed or unresolved measurement decision.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Row-level reason field.","grader_hint":"The reason must identify the source problem without inventing a correction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX records the reason for each irrelevant-row exclusion.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Row-level reason field.","grader_hint":"The reason must distinguish irrelevance from a measurement failure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX controlled-face count equals the source-derived distinct usable non-duplicate count, within ±0 records.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary and row-level register.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from included rows after all exception decisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX controlled-face minimum equals the source-derived minimum, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary and included rows.","grader_hint":"Use the same population as R43."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX controlled-face maximum equals the source-derived maximum, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary and included rows.","grader_hint":"Use the same population as R43."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX controlled-face mean equals the source-derived arithmetic mean, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary and included rows.","grader_hint":"Recalculate from unrounded included measurements where available."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX explicitly compares the controlled-face maximum with the supplied tolerance and shows that the maximum does not exceed it.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Summary or conclusion fields.","grader_hint":"Require both operands and a clear pass relationship, not just a 'pass' label."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX contains a visible conclusion field stating that the rejected parts conform under the supplied award documents.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook conclusion area.","grader_hint":"The conclusion must agree with the DOCX and be visible without inspecting formulas."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX contains a visible scope or limitation note restricting the conclusion to supplied documents and evidence.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook method or notes area.","grader_hint":"Check agreement with the letter's scope statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX discloses Tadeo Okonkwo's fixture-design role.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook disclosure or method area.","grader_hint":"The disclosure must be visible in the delivered workbook."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX explains an evidence-selection safeguard addressing the designer's potential conflict.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook method or disclosure area.","grader_hint":"Require a concrete reproducible safeguard, not merely the word 'independent'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the affirmative conformity conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Conclusion text in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Compare the operative conclusion, not just whether both contain the word 'conform'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the governing controlled surface and its distinction from the as-welded surface.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Reasoning and normalized fields in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"Both must identify the finished machined face as controlling and treat as-welded readings separately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the controlled-face count, within ±0 records.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter summary compared with workbook summary.","grader_hint":"The shared figure must match exactly after any displayed rounding convention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the controlled-face maximum, within ±0.01 mm.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter and workbook summaries compared with source.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated maximum using the specified tolerance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the stated flatness tolerance and unit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter, workbook, and PDF.","grader_hint":"Both deliverables must use the supplied value and unit, not merely equivalent wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the treatment of as-welded measurements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Letter reasoning compared with workbook decisions.","grader_hint":"Both must exclude them from the contractual calculation for the same source-grounded reason."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX and XLSX agree on the fixture-design disclosure and the stated insulation safeguard.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":true,"required":false,"evidence":"Disclosure sections in both deliverables.","grader_hint":"A disclosure in only one deliverable does not satisfy this cross-file agreement item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The DOCX reads as a usable professional opinion letter: the conclusion is easy to find, the reasoning is sequenced from governing document to evidence to conclusion, and the tone is decisive without overstating the evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX reviewed as a whole.","grader_hint":"Assess practical usability for Noor Maldonado's claim meeting; penalize hedging, buried conclusion, unsupported advocacy, or a report-like dump of raw rows."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The XLSX is usable as an evidence register: a reviewer can follow source location, normalized interpretation, exception treatment, inclusion decision, and summary without reverse-engineering hidden logic.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook reviewed as a whole.","grader_hint":"Assess traceability, readable labels, visible method, and coherent summary; technically correct but opaque work should not receive full credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R61","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered XLSX contains no #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! errors.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Formula and displayed-cell inspection.","grader_hint":"Inspect formulas and cached/displayed values across all worksheets."},{"rubric_item_id":"R62","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered DOCX contains no visible spreadsheet error tokens or unresolved placeholders such as #REF!, #DIV/0!, #VALUE!, or bracketed drafting text.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Extracted and rendered DOCX text.","grader_hint":"Search the complete document text and rendered pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R63","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The XLSX preserves the source evidence values and notes in traceable form without silently rewriting the source record.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Register compared with source workbook.","grader_hint":"Normalization may be added in separate fields, but original source value or text must remain recoverable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R64","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The final summaries use only included, usable, non-duplicate controlled-face records and do not count the unrelated side table.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook population and formulas/values compared with source layout.","grader_hint":"Reconcile summary population to the actual evidence table and exclusion decisions; side-table rows must contribute zero."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Fernhollow Systems supplied weld fixtures for Sandpiper Supply's chassis line, and Sandpiper is rejecting parts against a flatness callout. Tadeo Okonkwo, the engineer who designed the fixture, must prepare a defensible position for the commercial team from the award-time drawing, tolerance text, and inspection bundle.","difficulty_sources":["Interpreting whether the flatness requirement applies to the as-welded assembly or the machined face from the supplied datum scheme","Separating valid inspection evidence from duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, and inconsistently labelled rows","Producing a committed commercial position while disclosing the engineer's involvement in the fixture design and explaining the independence safeguard","Keeping the written opinion and spreadsheet evidence register aligned"],"authoring_plan":{"mode":"copy","source_count":2,"source_design":{"award_drawing_and_tolerance.pdf":{"content":["Create an award-time drawing extract for a chassis fixture and a companion tolerance note in the same PDF.","The drawing identifies datum A as the finished machined face and datum B and datum C as the locating features used after machining.","The feature control frame applies a flatness tolerance of 0.18 mm to the finished machined face; the welding sequence precedes machining, and the as-welded assembly face is not the controlled finished surface.","The drawing contains a note that the supplied award drawing and tolerance text are the governing contract documents for this review.","Use a drawing identifier, revision, feature labels, and issue date that can be copied into both deliverables."]},"inspection_bundle.xlsx":{"content":["Create a mixed-format inspection export with a real evidence table and an unrelated side table on the same worksheet.","Place a banner block above the evidence and gutter columns to the left so the real table does not begin at A1.","Put a line break inside one header of the unrelated side table; the side table must be clearly unrelated to conformance evidence and must not be treated as inspection data.","The evidence table contains source identifiers, part identifiers, surface labels, datum references, measured flatness, units, disposition, and a free-text notes field.","Include repeated records for the same part and inspection event, with one row being a duplicate or less complete copy; the evidence register must avoid double counting it.","Include at least one malformed measurement entry that cannot support a numeric comparison, at least one irrelevant row from another inspection characteristic or unrelated item, and inconsistent labels such as 'finished face', 'machined surface', and 'as-welded face'.","Use the notes field for row-level exceptions that override the main columns. At least one row whose main status or surface label looks eligible must be excluded because its note identifies it as a setup check or non-production piece. At least one row must remain unresolved or blank rather than receive an invented measurement because the note or source does not support a valid reading.","Provide valid readings on the controlled machined face and separate readings on the as-welded face. The valid controlled-face readings must all be at or below 0.18 mm; at least one as-welded reading must exceed 0.18 mm, creating the central inspection-basis trap.","Include rejection records that appear to support Sandpiper's position but are measurements of the as-welded surface or otherwise not valid evidence against the drawing-controlled feature.","Include enough valid controlled-face records to support a summary count, maximum, minimum, and arithmetic mean, with values selected by the build agent and derived by script rather than hand-entered into the gold.","Ensure all facts are text-extractable and do not introduce formula errors or any additional seeded defect beyond the specified banner, gutters, side table with embedded line break, notes overrides, duplicates, malformed entries, irrelevant rows, and inconsistent labels."]}},"transformation_and_verdict":{"worker_action":"Read the award drawing and tolerance text, locate and normalize the actual evidence table in the workbook, apply professional judgment to map labels to the drawing-controlled surface, use notes as row-level exceptions, exclude duplicate and irrelevant evidence, mark malformed or unsupported records without inventing measurements, and produce a committed opinion plus a traceable register.","intended_verdict":"The rejected parts conform under the supplied award drawing and tolerance text, because the contractual flatness callout governs the finished machined face and the valid controlled-face readings are within the stated tolerance. Measurements on the as-welded face do not establish nonconformance against that callout.","required_disclosures":["The opinion must say that Tadeo Okonkwo designed the fixture under review.","It must explain that the review was insulated by applying the award documents and an evidence-selection method consistently, with the commercial or quality team able to reproduce the register, rather than relying on the designer's unsupported assurance.","It must identify that the conclusion is limited to the supplied award documents and inspection evidence."]},"gold_derivation":"Use an offline script to parse the source workbook, identify the actual evidence table by headers rather than position, normalize surface labels, apply notes overrides, remove duplicate event records, exclude irrelevant and malformed records from numeric summaries, and calculate the valid controlled-face count, minimum, maximum, and mean. The reference solution should copy source facts into the letter and register, use the scripted summaries, and reach the intended verdict without adding external rules."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_drawing_tolerance","filename":"award_drawing_and_tolerance.pdf","purpose":"Award-time drawing extract and tolerance text governing the chassis fixture, including the datum reference frame, manufacturing sequence, surface identification, and contractual scope.","required":true,"discovery":"Read this before deciding which physical surface the flatness callout governs; it is the only supplied drawing and tolerance basis."},{"artifact_id":"ref_inspection_bundle","filename":"inspection_bundle.xlsx","purpose":"Mixed inspection and rejection evidence supplied by the quality team, including measurement rows, notes, labels, status fields, and an unrelated contact table placed beside the evidence table.","required":true,"discovery":"Inspect the whole workbook, including the banner, gutters, side table, headers, notes, and row-level records; do not assume the evidence table starts at cell A1."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"opinion_letter","filename":"sandpiper_conformance_opinion.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise conformance opinion letter for Noor Maldonado containing a committed conclusion, source basis, evidence treatment, limitations, and conflict-of-interest disclosure.","required":true,"constraints":["Use only facts supported by the two supplied reference files.","State a clear yes-or-no position on conformity under the award documents.","Identify the applicable drawing feature, datum scheme, tolerance, inspection basis, exclusions, and material limitations.","Disclose Tadeo Okonkwo's role in designing the fixture and explain the safeguard used to insulate the review.","Make every figure and factual statement shared with the workbook agree with it.","Do not cite external standards or invent customer concessions, dates, people, organisations, or measurements."],"rendering_required":true},{"deliverable_id":"evidence_register","filename":"sandpiper_conformance_register.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A traceable evidence register showing the source rows considered, normalized labels, inclusion or exclusion decisions, reasons, measurements, and the basis for the final conclusion.","required":true,"constraints":["Retain traceability to source row identifiers or equivalent source locations.","Show how duplicate, malformed, irrelevant, and inconsistently labelled records were handled.","Distinguish the drawing-controlled inspection surface from measurements taken on another surface.","Do not silently invent values for unusable records.","Make all summary figures and conclusion fields agree with the opinion letter.","Avoid external data and do not reproduce the unrelated contact table as inspection evidence."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"professional_report","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"mechanical_engineers","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"One domain-experienced reviewer checks the drawing interpretation and rendered letter; an independent offline script checks row inclusion, duplicate handling, summary metrics, and cross-deliverable figures; a second reviewer checks usability and conflict disclosure.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The task evaluates interpretation of the supplied drawing extract and evidence bundle only; it does not establish conformity under any later revision or external standard.","Rendered-office-library differences may affect pagination slightly, so review focuses on readable sequencing and visible content rather than exact page breaks."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:45+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:45+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:45+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:45+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R48']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T18:47:45+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/345ff9b5b21e3cd8","declared_deliverables":["sandpiper_conformance_opinion.docx","sandpiper_conformance_register.xlsx"]};
